From d44de1023b80bec492a831550b66014a802b6a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:22:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: do not clear xstats in stmmac_open()

The 6.1.191 backport of upstream 38cc3c6dcc09 ("net: stmmac: protect
updates of 64-bit statistics counters") moved the interrupt counters to
the per-CPU xstats.pcpu_stats, allocated in stmmac_dvr_probe(). The
6.1.y stmmac_open() still clears the whole struct stmmac_extra_stats,
which sets pcpu_stats to NULL, so the first DMA interrupt after the
interface comes up oopses in u64_stats_inc() (dwmac4_dma_interrupt).

Mainline dropped this memset in 133466c3bbe1 ("net: stmmac: use
per-queue 64 bit statistics where necessary"); do the same.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index 7bc75e997..613cb2e89 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -3830,8 +3830,6 @@ static int __stmmac_open(struct net_device *dev,
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* Extra statistics */
-	memset(&priv->xstats, 0, sizeof(struct stmmac_extra_stats));
 	priv->xstats.threshold = tc;
 
 	priv->rx_copybreak = STMMAC_RX_COPYBREAK;
-- 
